  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in Montana through FY2026 to date totals $1B in obligations. The federal government issued 6,536 awards in the period, with an average award size of $154K. Obligations fell 12.3% year over year. Fiscal-year totals are partial and represent contract obligations to date. Montana’s five-year series shows obligations of $691M in FY21, $925M in FY22, $1B in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, $1.1B in FY25, and $1B in FY26, indicating where current-year activity sits relative to recent years. Contracting spans transportation, construction, services, and manufacturing. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest industry by obligations at $167M, followed by Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $137M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $124M. The Department of Defense, Department of Agriculture, and Department of Homeland Security are the leading buyers, while S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC, BRIDGER AIR TANKER LLC, and ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV are the top vendors by obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year in Montana federal contracting?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 12.3% year over year. Total obligations in FY2026 to date are $1B, matching the FY23 total but below FY24 and FY25 levels of $1.1B. The number of awards is 6,536, with an average award size of $154K, showing how spending and transaction counts combine in the partial fiscal year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate Montana federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $327M, the Department of Agriculture obligated $263M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $173M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest industry with $167M, Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance follows with $137M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is third with $124M."
      }
    ]
  },
